NAME
====

**wattle-apps** - manage installed applications

SYNOPSIS
========

**wattle apps** _verb_ [_argument_]

DESCRIPTION
===========

**wattle apps** manages installed applications. An *application* is a project
with executable programs for installation. See `wattle-applications(7)` for
the application layout and installation requirements.

Each application is installed in `lib/wattle/apps/<group>/<name>/` under
``*prefix*``. Programs are installed in `bin/` and manual pages in
`share/man/`. An application's modules are not made available for import by
other applications.

A build made without the OS library does not include ***apps***. Each verb
reports this limitation and exits with status 1. **a** is a synonym for
***apps***.

VERBS
=====

- ***install*** [_source_ [_ref_]]:
  Install an application. _source_ is a directory, a name ending in ``.tar`` or
  ``.tar.gz``, or a Git repository. A directory is installed as it is. A name
  ending in ``.tar`` or ``.tar.gz`` is downloaded with **curl** and unpacked
  with **tar**. Anything else is cloned with **git**. With no _source_, the
  current directory is installed. The application's info file requires
  ``:name`` and ``:group``. The group is conventionally a reverse domain such
  as ``net.inqk``. Installed application names are unique across groups.

  The project declares the programs to install under ``:exes``. Native
  executables are built and installed in `bin/`. Source executables are
  copied with a program in `bin/` that runs them. Associated libraries and
  manual pages are installed with the programs. Web executables are not
  installed. An application script, if present, replaces this installation
  with custom hooks. See `wattle-applications(7)`.

  _ref_ specifies a branch or tag and applies only to a Git repository.

- ***upgrade*** [_name_]:
  Install the application _name_ again from the source it was installed from.
  An application installed from a tarball or a Git repository is downloaded
  again. With no _name_, every installed application is upgraded.

- ***remove*** _name_:
  Remove the application _name_.

- ***list***:
  List the installed applications.

EXAMPLES
========

Install applications from a directory, a tarball and a Git repository, and list
the installed applications:

````
$ wattle apps install ./my-app
$ wattle apps install https://example.com/my-app.tar.gz
$ wattle apps install https://example.com/my-app.git v1.2
$ wattle apps list
````

Install every application again from its source, and remove one:

````
$ wattle apps upgrade
$ wattle apps remove my-app
````

SEE ALSO
========

`wattle(1)`, `wattle-build(1)`, `wattle-deps(1)`, `wattle-applications(7)`
